RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       If  _s is not NULL, the mmbbttoowwcc() function returns the number of consumed
       bytes starting at _s, or 0 if _s points to a null byte, or -1 upon  fail‐
       ure.

       If _s is NULL, the mmbbttoowwcc() function returns nonzero if the encoding has
       nontrivial shift state, or zero if the encoding is stateless.

